  "directAnswer": "Based on the time of supply rules under Section 11 of the Goods and Services Tax Act 1993, a supply of goods or services takes place at the earlier of when an invoice is issued or when payment is received. Since the invoice was issued in December 2022 (earlier than the payment received in January 2023), the time of supply occurs in December 2022. Therefore, the GST rate applicable to supplies made in December 2022 (7%) applies.",
  "keyRules": [
    "Section 11 of the Goods and Services Tax Act 1993 states that a supply of goods or services is treated as taking place at the time when an invoice in respect of the supply is issued, or when any payment in respect of the supply is received by the supplier, whichever is the earlier.",
    "Section 16 of the Goods and Services Tax Act 1993 specifies that the GST rate was 7% for the period from 1 July 2007 to 31 December 2022, and 8% for the period from 1 January 2023 to 31 December 2023."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Assumes the invoice issued in December 2022 is a valid tax invoice representing a genuine supply.",
    "Specific transitional rules may apply if the supply spans across the rate change period or involves specific continuous supplies or prepayments."
